  6. THE SIBLING LADDER: the residual measured against how many siblings the removed electron had

     Every corridor row is an INNER-SHELL removal the store carries as a later ionisation limit of
     the neutral, so the electron leaves a shell that still holds siblings.  Sibling energy is the
     converged second-order pair correlation it loses (siblingpair.py, LMAX = 5).

     row     el  siblings   predicted   measured   residual        sibling E   undelivered
